            <p class="panel-note">{c["after"]}</p>
            <img class="shot" src="{after_src}" alt="After: {c["title"]}" loading="lazy">
          </figure>
        </div>
      </section>""")

    return f"""<title>Behavior output visibility — UI proof</title>
<style>{CSS}</style>
<div class="wrap">
  <header class="masthead">
    <p class="eyebrow">Owletto pointer proof · lobu#2590 + owletto#746</p>
    <h1>A Behavior's own output was invisible to the Behavior page</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Agent runs stamped their output <code>occurred_at = window_end</code>. For a sub-daily
      Behavior that timestamp sits in the future all day, and every read path carries an
      <code>occurred_at &lt;= now()</code> guard — so a Behavior's page showed the prompt and
      nothing else. That same future stamp was also the only thing stopping a Behavior from
      re-reading its own output, which is why the fix is a pair: attribute output at write
      time (<code>events.behavior_id</code>), exclude self from the window by attribution
      rather than by clock, and clamp the stamp to <code>min(window_end, now())</code>.
      Both shots below come from the same booted app, one Owletto checkout apart.
    </p>
    <div class="facts">{facts}</div>
  </header>
  {"".join(cases)}
  <footer class="colophon">
    <p>Captured 2026-08-08 against a local server on the same database, restarting only the
      Owletto checkout between the before and after pass. Counts in the second case were read
      from the rendered page: <code>?produced_by=8</code> returns 7 of 12 events.</p>
    <p>Not covered by these shots: the extracted <code>EventsFeed</code> also backs the Memory
      events tab and the peek pane; those were verified by test, not by screenshot.</p>
  </footer>
</div>
"""


